  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Provincial Competitiveness Index (PCI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Vietnam):  .The Provincial Competitiveness Index (PCI) facilitates an improved business enabling environment driving greater competitiveness and private sector growth through advances in governance at the provincial level. Nearly two decades old, PCI produces a province-by-province competitiveness score that is widely watched by the public and private sectors. ..With FY 2021 funds, the PCI activity will: 1) identify obstacles and barriers to doing business through surveys of domestic and foreign invested firms; 2) analyzing governance data and proposing recommendations for reforms to policy makers and local authorities through policy dialogues; 3) improving local governance capacity by increasing the availability of data on governance through reports, diagnostic workshops, training, best practice sharing, website and e-newsletters; and 4) supporting Vietnam Chamber of Commerce and Industry in developing a Green Index to improve the regulatory environment reforms and create public-private partnership (PPP) opportunities to respond to mutual interest of improving environmentally-friendly investment at provincial level. This will help the U.S. Businesses choose provinces that are focusing on the application of green technologies and green practices, and willingness to invest in green operations. ..These efforts will result in policy and process improvement and reforms at the provincial level that will help create a more competitive and transparent business environment for better investment and trade. It will also boost Vietnam&apos;s competitiveness, expand market opportunities for U.S. markets, and elevate environmental policy..This activity supports Vietnam to promote greater transparency, investment and trade opportunities, and encouraging a business-enabling environment leading to upper-middle income status. In addition, the activity supports the Indo-Pacific framework by creating the business enabling environment necessary to scale up foreign and domestic investments.</narrative>
  </description>
